    ],
    "lyrics": {
      "text": "By the in-ter-ces-sions of Thy Mar-tyrs, O Lord, grant rest un-to the souls of Thy serv-ants.\n\nHav-ing stead-fast-ly strug-gled in___ your mar-tyr-ic fights, with in-ef-fa-ble crowns of vic---t’ry are ye a-dorned, O prize-win-ning Mar-tyrs of Christ, as to Christ ye shout: Thee do we su-preme--ly ex-alt to all__ the ag-es.\n\nTheir souls shall dwell a-mong good__ things.\n\nDo Thou kind-ly re-ceive the faith---ful who sa-cred-ly have for-sak-en this life and passed___ on to Thee, the Lord, grant-ing them that rest, see-ing Thou art com-pas-sion-ate, as they all ex-alt__ Thee, O Christ, to all__ the ag-es.\n\nWe bless Fa-ther, Son, and Ho-ly Spir-it, the Lord.\n\nIn the land of the meek as-sign___ now their dwell-ing-place un-to all who be-fore have fall---en a-sleep till now, jus-ti-fied by Thee through their faith in Thee and by grace, as they all ex-alt__ Thee, O Sav-iour, to__ the ag-es.\n\nBoth now and ev--er, and un-to the ag--es of ag-es. A-men.\n\nO_ all-blest, we all call thee bless---ed, who gav-est birth to the Word Who in-deed is bless---ed in ver-y truth, Who for our sal-va-tion be-came flesh as mor-tal man. Him do we su-preme--ly ex-alt to all__ the ag-es.\n\nWe praise, we bless, and we wor-ship the Lord.\n\nFrom the flame didst Thou gush forth dew___ on the right-eous Youths, and with wa-ter didst burn the just___ man’s sac-ri-fice; for Thou, O Christ, do-est all things by Thy will a-lone. Thee do we su-preme--ly ex-alt to all__ the ag-es."
    }
  }
}